  "subject": "A husband who stormed out over selling the old rattan chair stands at the last card-phone booth outside Tainan station with a dead mobile and one unit left on his phone card, dials the only number he remembers, cannot speak, and hears her tell him not to hang up.",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien 1960s nightclub slow-waltz ballad in 3/4, Taiwanese kayokyoku-era feel. String section sustaining long legato lines; clarinet playing a sighing countermelody with vibrato; nylon-string guitar arpeggiating the waltz; upright bass on beat one; brushed drums on a soft three-count; piano filling gently between lines. Warm vintage 1960s studio mix, light tape sheen, plain close vocal with short room reverb. Male baritone, warm with slow vibrato, clearly sung melody, one lead voice. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 84 BPM, A minor. Tender, tongue-tied mood, relieved at the end. No rap, no trap hi-hats, no autotune, no synth pads, no electric guitar distortion, no EDM drop.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n電話亭 徛佇車頭邊\n我的手機 電攏無去\n袋仔內 干焦一張電話卡\n顯示的字 賰上尾一格\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我袂記得別人的號碼\n干焦這一組 四十年無換\n\n[Chorus]\n喂 是我 我毋是欲吵\n嘟嘟聲咧催 錢欲用完\n喂 你若敢聽 就免講話\n聽我的喘氣 就知我佇遮\n\n[Verse]\n透早為著一張舊藤椅\n我講欲賣 你講免賣\n我大聲講話 就挵門出去\n連外套 都囥佇椅仔頂\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n卡仔咧叫 賰十秒鐘\n我的喙 閣是拍結\n\n[Chorus]\n喂 是我 這擺是我毋著\n嘟嘟聲咧催 錢欲用完\n喂 你若敢聽 就免講話\n聽我的喘氣 就知我佇遮\n\n[Verse]\n電話彼頭 你先開喙\n你講 我知 是你 莫掛\n藤椅仔無賣矣 外套我提咧\n你猶佇門口 等我\n\n[Bridge]\n嘟 一聲 卡仔吐出來\n這擺 換你共我講\n\n[Chorus]\n喂 是你 免驚 我就轉去\n卡仔吐出來 錢攏用完\n喂 你若敢聽 免等我到\n我行路轉去 十分鐘\n\n[Outro]\n上尾一格 用完矣\n電話亭外口 月娘光",
